          "guid": "mrzmazadnr5e8oo7",
          "message": {
            "text": "pauseAnimations is opt-in (default false) SPECIFICALLY so svg-scrubber is excluded. The scrubber shares htmlWrapper (src/scrubber/server.ts) but has a PLAY mode that needs the animation to actually run — pinning animation-play-state: paused globally would freeze it. The frame-EXPORT paths (svg-to-video, svg-to-image) only ever seek, so they pass true to harden the FIRST exported frame against the DM-1779 backward-seek tear (a free-run before the first seek, then seeking back to frame 0). svg-scrubber's interactive per-step scrubbing re-renders cleanly, so it doesn't need the pin. Verified: svg-to-image-e2e (paused export) and scrubber server.e2e (play mode) both green.\n",
            "markdown": "`pauseAnimations` is opt-in (default false) SPECIFICALLY so svg-scrubber is excluded. The scrubber shares `htmlWrapper` (src/scrubber/server.ts) but has a PLAY mode that needs the animation to actually run — pinning `animation-play-state: paused` globally would freeze it. The frame-EXPORT paths (svg-to-video, svg-to-image) only ever seek, so they pass true to harden the FIRST exported frame against the DM-1779 backward-seek tear (a free-run before the first seek, then seeking back to frame 0). svg-scrubber's interactive per-step scrubbing re-renders cleanly, so it doesn't need the pin. Verified: svg-to-image-e2e (paused export) and scrubber server.e2e (play mode) both green.\n"
          },
